e something that  left some people  a bit worried since as vast as the  overworld was  pretty much every nook and cranny of  this landscape has been scrutinized in  the past 4 years  what else is there to do at this point  more quests a new story event and yet  even more shrines will probably not be  enough to avoid the game from feeling  like the dlc it was originally intended  to be  so naturally once we saw lincoln zelda  traversing a vast cave we concluded that  hyrule may have a wide array of caves  underground ruins and maybe even entire  subterranean cities to explore  another widely discussed idea is  underwater exploration  and for good reason many zelda games  have featured it in the past  horizon is doing it for its sequel and  given the fact that breath the wild was  all about player freedom not being able  to venture beneath the waves of hyrule's  lakes and oceans was definitely one of a  few restrictions that clashed with the  open world design philosophy  apart from petting dogs and no i'm never  gonna let this go  who's a good boy who's your good boy  you are yes you are alright alright i'm  gonna let this go  for now so we have underground and  underwater  both of which feature descending down on  the z-axis assuming the zelda team won't  expand the map beyond its current  borders that leaves us with one more  direction to go  after all the z-axis doesn't only go  down but up  as well now i'm definitely not the first  to pitch this  idea people have been calling for the  return of loft wings or returned to  skyloft and even outer space in some  cases since the very beginning but what  i want to do today is show you some  interesting speculation  hints and observations that other people  have pointed out to me in the past weeks  as well as give you some of my own takes  on the matter that shows that gameplay  featuring aviation  could be a possibility because when you  think about it  for a game that calls itself open air  rather than the traditional  open world there wasn't really all that  much to the sky  in breath of the wild sure paragliding  around was nice  but other than that it's mostly just a  case of holding forward on the control  stick  airborne enemies were often conveniently  hovering only a few feet off the ground  the only exceptions were the floating  platforms which were only present in  master mode and part of dlc pack 1 and  some very specific scripted events such  as  entering valmeado and the fight with the  malice-infested nadra both of which  required the use of perpetual updrafts  which weren't there under normal  circumstances  and this is not meant to be a criticism  of breath of the wild there was a lot to  explore on the surface which is where  the main focus lies the paraglider was  there to make traversal faster  more fun to do and encourage climbing to  high places and finding vantage points  back in 2017 its inclusion was pretty  novel  rarely had we seen this level of freedom  before being able to glide around from  anywhere to anywhere was amazing but as  was to be expected since then  other games have started to implement  similar mechanics like gentian impact  and even horizon forbidden west recently  revealed a similar feature  because of this and the fact that breath  the wild is four years old now the  mechanic  doesn't feel as special anymore but as  stated before this  isn't about breath the wild but it's  sequel and for the sequel we need more  than just a few new landmarks to explore  so next i want to talk about a few  things a the means by which link can  take flight  b the possible story implications and  see some additional gameplay elements  that could come into play  if this is realized the paraglider was  designed to slowly descend  not ascend so it either needs to get an  upgrade that does allow link to soar  upwards like rivale's go except not  restricted to a single grounded boost  or a completely new power mount or  device to do so  one option i discussed with andre's  restart on his podcast not too long ago  was the return  of loftwings i've been very skeptical  about the idea of loftwing's returning  since nintendo rarely brings back  central mechanics from previous titles  there are exceptions like phantom  hourglass revisiting wind waker sailing  but this doesn't happen often the wall  merging mechanic from a link between  worlds the mass transformations from  majora's mask wolfling travelling by  train  none of these have ever made a return in  the same way that's kind of the way  nintendo rolls  they come up with a unique central  mechanic and then it's gone afterwards  some may see this as a negative but at  the same time it's also what still gives  the zelda series its right to exist  even after more than 20 installments  however there is one thing that made me  more open to the possibility of  loftwings that being the recent  introduction of the loftwing amiibo now  do i think loftwings will play a central  role in breath of the wild 2  no but it could at least be possible  that it will unlock something extra and  before you start sweating because you  can't or won't buy the loftwing amiibo  i'm not saying that this will be the  only way to obtain a loft wing  instead you could compare it to a pona  who was only available through amiibo  but  other horses still exist so perhaps the  amiibo will unlock link's crimson  loftwing from skyward sword as a reward  for buying the amiibo  if loftwings were to make a return in  breathtak 2 this would be only one of a  few times that nintendo has brought back  a core mechanic from a previous game but  in this case i think it would be totally  justified  because as those of you who've already  played skyward sword know this was a  very underdeveloped aspect of the game  ever since the review of skyward sword  the main selling point which got the  most attention beside the motion  controls was flying around on your bird  but there wasn't really all that much to  it there were no enemies to fight in the  sky  heck link couldn't even use any of his  weapons while airborne  all the loftwing was good for was  landing on things and as a way to reach  the surface  that's it i think breathtak 2 could do  so much more with this concept  that being said this doesn't mean it has  to be achieved through the use of loft  wings of course  there are other alternatives an obvious  one would be a return to the sheikah  tech once more  the master cycle zero demonstrated the  superiority of the shika technology for  traverso  on land so what if this time around link  obtains a new vehicle that can fly  perhaps built by robbie or pura a device  which can be upgraded as you progress  through the main story similar to the  master cycle it may require fuel and at  first the amount of air time you can get  out of it is limited but similar to the  stamina gauge  upgrades can make it fly longer or  higher as you go  in creating a champion we can see that  nintendo was initially thinking about  the inclusion of vials or  syringes filled with ancient energy by  the looks of it they were meant to power  the sheikah slade but i guess that got  scrapped to make use of the slate more  convenient without having to fill it up  each time but for a vehicle  portable and obtainable ancient energy  would make perfect sense  another option which we already got a  very brief glimpse of could be link's  magic spirit arm  we still have no idea what this means  for the gameplay but if we do some wild  speculation here  what if this is what grants linked the  power of temporary flight it could  either manipulate link's paraglider  allowing him to ascend while  gliding or perhaps link won't even need  a paraglider and the hand allows him to  superman his way around for short  periods of time i know this sounds crazy  but  i mean whatever this being is it seems  to house itself  or its power into link and if this being  turns out to be a sage or maybe  even a twilight both of which have shown  to be able to hover or fly  perhaps this ability is bestowed upon  link similar to how rivali's essence  gave him access to his ability this also  got me thinking  if you look closely at the teaser link  seems to be keeling backwards as the  hand latches on to him  this could of course mean nothing but at  the same time what if this is how it  saves link and zelda in this scenario  it's pretty clear that the two are in  serious danger of falling down the  bottomless pit surrounding ganon's  corpse  so what if they do fall down and the  hand saves them by giving link its power  of flight this could mean that during  this shot link is either  already falling possibly with zelda  right below him and he gains the power  mid-fall so he can save her  and himself or he's in the process of  going over the edge at this moment  either way similar to the shika flying  machine this power  obviously has to be limited maybe it  runs on magic which means we could see a  return of the magic meter  upgrading the meter would then mean  being able to fly for longer  so these are a few possibilities as to  how so now let's go over the why  why would link need to fly if there's  nothing to do in the sky anyway  some floating platforms and flying  enemies are certainly not  enough for such a huge addition to the  gameplay well as you've probably guessed  the rising hyrule castle could  definitely have something to do with it  which is also where i need to address  something that bannon pointed out to me  on twitter he claims that the castle  isn't the only thing rising up in the  final shot but an area called the  bottomless swamp as well  now i gotta be honest this might just be  part of the overworld fog we often see  rolling around in hyrule's landscape but  if you look closely you definitely do  see a pretty significant  cloud rising up in this area at the same  time the castle is rising up there's  also a big cloud formation in front of  the castle which would approximately be  where the central chica tower would have  been again could be nothing more than  just some random clouds which just so  happen  to form at this exact moment but it's  not too crazy to think that hyrule  castle isn't the only thing rising but  instead multiple sections of hyrule will  take to the skies  creating an entire cluster of floating  islands above the map and leaving  enormous craters where they once  were i'd also like to point out that  it's a bit weird that the screen is  shaking so viciously when whatever is  happening to the castle  is that far away in fact the shaking  doesn't start until way later perhaps an  indication that the great plateau itself  which is where this footage is taken  from  is about to rise up as well i definitely  love the idea of multiple floating  islands and not like in skyward sword  where they were mostly just a bunch of  floating rocks  i mean actual big chunks of land with  waterfalls  vegetation maybe even entire villages  that got taken to the sky with it  i mean can you imagine the shock the  people of hatano village or the gorons  would endure if something like this were  to happen to them  one little hint to the possibility of  multiple floating islands is the concept  art shown at the gdc  the one where ganondorf is standing on a  giant floating landmass  and as you may notice this is not the  castle floating but rather seems to be  death mountain we of course can also not  forget the mothership high up in the sky  with smaller vessels around it  not saying aliens will be the main bad  guy i doubt we'll get ganondorf  and aliens but it at least shows that  the team was toying around with enemies  high up in the sky  it could be that vametto was the  replacement of that idea but  i just want to cover all options and  speaking of vametto  age of calamity already gave us a taste  of some airborne combat in the vametto  sections  and i don't know about you but i thought  these were pretty darn cool  your range of motion was severely  limited as was the area you were allowed  to fly in but it at least shows that the  vast open space above hyrule's map lends  itself for huge aerial battles  so in terms of story it could be that  ganondorf rips parts of hyrule asunder  and elevates them to the sky  each of these islands could be hovering  at different elevations and thus the  journey to ganondorf's castle could be  hindered by how far your powers and gear  allow you to ascend  upwards meanwhile back at the surface  new challenges are awaiting as well  perhaps the craters left behind by the  land that rose up reveals underground  caves which could tie into the  underground stuff  add to that the possibility of  underwater traversal and subtly  revisiting the same map again  doesn't seem as redundant anymore this  world would be turned on its head and  new provinces wouldn't even be necessary  an example of a story progression in  this case would be that as ganondorf  took himself and parts of hyrule to the  sky you are basically stuck on the  ground at first  unable to do much which would be similar  to the great plateau in breath the wild  where link was stuck  until he obtains the paraglider and you  can start the main quest proper  in this case you wouldn't be able to  leave the surface until you obtain your  first ability to fly be it a loft wing  ashika vehicle or the green spirit hand  which then at first allows you to visit  some of the  lower hanging islands from there you  advance further and further upwards by  beating dungeons upgrade your power to  fly and obtain new abilities  speaking of which let's lastly do a  quick dive into some additional gameplay  options which could work well with the  idea of aviation  obviously a hook shot or grapple hook  would make a fine addition to this  i've already talked about something like  this in the past but something that  worried me was being able to hit  exact targets while falling or flying  might be a bit too difficult then i  suddenly remembered another mechanic  which was introduced in breath the wild  the bullet time being able to slow down  time mid-air would give you ample amount  of time needed to hit your targets  other mechanics could include the option  to actually use your weapons while  flying  something which wasn't possible with the  paraglider since link needed both hands  to hold on  being able to deploy a small flying  device similar to the beetle something  we have seen nintendo contemplating on  two occasions  in creating a champion maybe the hens  power can give link a double jump  similar to rox cape from minish cap to  get some extra distance  or creating your own platforms in the  air like the cloud power-up from mario  galaxy 2.  the list goes on now it could be that  all the stuff i'm describing is  way too ambitious and it isn't without  its problems either  we've seen how in breath the wild people  were able to utterly break the game by  abusing the physics engine  stuff like this would definitely make  sequence breaking the game a breeze  given that it has a certain order in  which you need to complete the main  story  so either these glitches if you can call  them that need to be removed or  since these were made possible because  of the sheikah slate the slate itself  would have to be retired it would of  course be amazing if we get it all  skye underwater and underground but like  i said that might be asking a bit too  much and i definitely don't want to set  anyone up for disappointment here  but we can dream can't we one thing's  for sure in order for the sequel to live  up to the hype and surpass the game of  the year winning breath of the wild  we're gonna need more than just some new  quests and new areas to what degree  that remains to be seen and that my  friends is the last of my thoughts and  speculations on breath of the wild 2.  now watch as this video becomes totally  irrelevant in one week's time  but hey at least we had fun coming up  with ideas these last two years  as you might expect this will be my last  video until after e3 is over however i  will be streaming the nintendo  presentation together with some of my  friends so i hope you will join me then  as we will make sure it will be a hype  and entertaining broadcast  until then this is dawn signing off  and have a good one  [Music]  [Music]  you

